# LLM visibility for public pages

Public HTML pages must be readable by LLMs/agents. Do not hand-wire discovery
in multiple places — extend the shared registry and page generator map.

## Source of truth

1. Add the page to `packages/shared-core/routes/app.ts` (`markdownPages`)
2. Add a Markdown generator in `apps/web/src/services/markdown/getPageMarkdown.ts`
   (`pageMarkdownGenerators` — TypeScript requires every registry path)

Path helpers, sitemap, `/llms.txt`, `/llms-full.txt`, Accept negotiation, and
`.md` rewrites all derive from that registry. Do **not** edit the proxy matcher
list for each new page.

## On the HTML page

```tsx
import { markdownAlternates } from '../../services/markdown/markdownAlternates';
import { MarkdownPageShell } from '../layouts/MarkdownPageShell';

export const metadata = {
  alternates: markdownAlternates(myRoute),
  title: '…',
};

export default function Page() {
  return <MarkdownPageShell path={myRoute}>{/* page content */}</MarkdownPageShell>;
}
```

## Do not

- Auth, API, webhook, or OAuth routes — leave them out of `markdownPages`
- Separate hand-maintained `.md` files that can drift from the HTML page
- `ai-content` / `llms` meta tags, User-Agent cloaking, or “for AI only” pages
- Per-page `/api/markdown` handlers — proxy rewrites to `/llm-markdown`

## Verify

- `turbo check:types` (generator map exhaustiveness)
- Unit tests under `services/markdown/__tests__` and `routes/__tests__`
